#: ../../../Proposals/VariableNames.md:168
msgid "Transition Options"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Proposals/VariableNames.md:170
msgid "There are three main options for transitioning:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Proposals/VariableNames.md:172
#: ../../../Proposals/VariableNames.md:176
msgid "Keep the current coding standard"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Proposals/VariableNames.md:173
#: ../../../Proposals/VariableNames.md:185
msgid "Laissez faire"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Proposals/VariableNames.md:174
#: ../../../Proposals/VariableNames.md:205
msgid "Big bang"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Proposals/VariableNames.md:178
msgid ""
"Proponents of keeping the current coding standard (i.e. not transitioning at "
"all) question whether the cost of transition outweighs the benefit "
"[^cite_emersonconcern] [^cite_reamesconcern] [^cite_bradburyconcern]. The "
"costs are that `git blame` will become less usable; and that merging the "
"changes will be costly for downstream maintainers. See [Big bang](#big-bang) "
"for potential mitigations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Proposals/VariableNames.md:187
msgid ""
"The coding standard could allow both `CamelCase` and `camelBack` styles for "
"variable names [^cite_lattnertransition]."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Proposals/VariableNames.md:190
msgid ""
"A code review to implement this is at <https://reviews.llvm.org/D57896>."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Proposals/VariableNames.md:192
msgid "Advantages"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Proposals/VariableNames.md:194
msgid "Very easy to implement initially."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Proposals/VariableNames.md:196
msgid "Disadvantages"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Proposals/VariableNames.md:198
msgid ""
"Leads to inconsistency [^cite_bradburyconcern] [^cite_aminiinconsistent]."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Proposals/VariableNames.md:199
msgid ""
"Inconsistency means it will be hard to know at a guess what name a variable "
"will have [^cite_dasinconsistent] [^cite_carruthinconsistent]."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Proposals/VariableNames.md:201
msgid ""
"Some large-scale renaming may happen anyway, leading to its disadvantages "
"without any mitigations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Proposals/VariableNames.md:207
msgid ""
"With this approach, variables will be renamed by an automated script in a "
"series of large commits."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Proposals/VariableNames.md:210
msgid ""
"The principle advantage of this approach is that it minimises the cost of "
"inconsistency [^cite_bradburytransition] [^cite_robinsontransition]."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Proposals/VariableNames.md:213
msgid ""
"It goes against a policy of avoiding large-scale reformatting of existing "
"code [^cite_greenedistinguish]."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Proposals/VariableNames.md:216
msgid ""
"It has been suggested that LLD would be a good starter project for the "
"renaming [^cite_ueyama]."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Proposals/VariableNames.md:219
msgid "Keeping git blame usable"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Proposals/VariableNames.md:221
msgid ""
"`git blame` (or `git annotate`) permits quickly identifying the commit that "
"changed a given line in a file. After renaming variables, many lines will "
"show as being changed by that one commit, requiring a further invocation of "
"`git blame` to identify prior, more interesting commits "
"[^cite_greenegitblame] [^cite_ricciacronyms]."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Proposals/VariableNames.md:227
msgid ""
"**Mitigation**: [git-hyper-blame](https://commondatastorage.googleapis.com/"
"chrome-infra-docs/flat/depot_tools/docs/html/git-hyper-blame.html) can "
"ignore or \"look through\" a given set of commits. A `.git-blame-ignore-"
"revs` file identifying the variable renaming commits could be added to the "
"LLVM git repository root directory. It is being [investigated](https://"
"public-inbox.org/git/20190324235020.49706-1-michael@platin.gs/) whether "
"similar functionality could be added to `git blame` itself."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Proposals/VariableNames.md:235
msgid "Minimising cost of downstream merges"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Proposals/VariableNames.md:237
msgid ""
"There are many forks of LLVM with downstream changes. Merging a large-scale "
"renaming change could be difficult for the fork maintainers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Proposals/VariableNames.md:240
msgid ""
"**Mitigation**: A large-scale renaming would be automated. A fork maintainer "
"can merge from the commit immediately before the renaming, then apply the "
"renaming script to their own branch. They can then merge again from the "
"renaming commit, resolving all conflicts by choosing their own version. This "
"could be tested on the [^cite_sve] fork."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Proposals/VariableNames.md:246
msgid "Provisional Plan"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Proposals/VariableNames.md:248
msgid ""
"This is a provisional plan for the [Big bang](#big-bang) approach. It has "
"not been agreed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Proposals/VariableNames.md:250
msgid ""
"Investigate improving `git blame`. The extent to which it can be made to "
"\"look through\" commits may impact how big a change can be made."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Proposals/VariableNames.md:253
msgid "Write a script to expand acronyms."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Proposals/VariableNames.md:255
msgid ""
"Experiment and perform dry runs of the various refactoring options. Results "
"can be published in forks of the LLVM Git repository."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Proposals/VariableNames.md:258
msgid "Consider the evidence and agree on the new policy."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Proposals/VariableNames.md:260
msgid "Agree & announce a date for the renaming of the starter project (LLD)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Proposals/VariableNames.md:262
msgid ""
"Update the [policy page](../CodingStandards.md). This will explain the old "
"and new rules and which projects each applies to."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Proposals/VariableNames.md:265
msgid "Refactor the starter project in two commits:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Proposals/VariableNames.md:267
msgid ""
"Add or change the project's .clang-tidy to reflect the agreed rules. (This "
"is in a separate commit to enable the merging process described in "
"[Minimising cost of downstream merges](#minimising-cost-of-downstream-"
"merges)). Also update the project list on the policy page."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Proposals/VariableNames.md:272
msgid ""
"Apply `clang-tidy` to the project's files, with only the `readability-"
"identifier-naming` rules enabled. `clang-tidy` will also reformat the "
"affected lines according to the rules in `.clang-format`. It is anticipated "
"that this will be a good dog-fooding opportunity for clang-tidy, and bugs "
"should be fixed in the process, likely including:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Proposals/VariableNames.md:278
msgid ""
"[readability-identifier-naming incorrectly fixes lambda capture](https://"
"bugs.llvm.org/show_bug.cgi?id=41119)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Proposals/VariableNames.md:279
msgid ""
"[readability-identifier-naming incorrectly fixes variables which become "
"keywords](https://bugs.llvm.org/show_bug.cgi?id=41120)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Proposals/VariableNames.md:281
msgid ""
"[readability-identifier-naming misses fixing member variables in destructor]"
"(https://bugs.llvm.org/show_bug.cgi?id=41122)."
msgstr ""

